# Security

- Secrets (Trello key/token, DB passwords, session secrets) live only in env / protected configuration outside Git.
- Do not commit `.env`; keep `.env.example` without real secrets.
- The API must not return integration secrets in plaintext.
- Store passwords only as secure hashes (when using local auth).
- Enforce permissions on the backend for every protected endpoint.
- Call Trello only from the backend.
- Logs must not contain tokens, passwords, or sensitive payloads.
- Configure CORS / cookies / HTTPS for the production domain; do not invent server details without surveying the real infrastructure.
- Do not change production Nginx/systemd config without an explicit task and impact check on other apps.
